course: dictionary
lesson: 5993
title: Meanness: unkind or stingy
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Meanness means being unkind or nasty to others. It can also mean not wanting to share or spend money, which is being stingy. Read the words around it to know which meaning fits. «Leo stared at the empty space where the kid had been and felt awful — he had just handed the meanness on, like a hot potato.» Here meanness is unkindness: Leo passed a nasty act on to someone else.
explain: Some words show you the sense straight away. «A spoiler tells the ending before someone has seen it; it is annoying, and spoiling on purpose is a small meanness that needs a "sorry".» A sorry is what you say when you have hurt someone, so meanness here means an unkind act.
explain: Meanness can be explained, but not excused. «Understanding why someone is mean does not make the meanness okay, but it can change how you respond.» You can understand why a person acts unkindly and still know that the act was wrong.
fact: Meanness is a noun, and it is uncountable: you cannot say "a meanness" in most sentences, only "some meanness" or "meanness".
fact: The first meaning is being unkind or nasty to others.
fact: The second meaning is not wanting to share or spend money; being stingy.
fact: In the UK, "mean" often means stingy, so meanness is often about money there. In the USA, it mostly means unkindness.
fact: Predators hunt to eat, not out of meanness, so meanness is a choice people make, not something every animal does.
exercise: «A friend keeps all the sweets and never shares, even when asked.» Which meaning of meanness fits here? | *Being stingy, not wanting to share | Speed | Kindness | Bravery
exercise: «Copying a mean player spreads the meanness to someone new.» What does spreads the meanness mean? | *Passes unkindness on to someone else | Makes the game faster | Gives a gift to everyone | Stops the game
exercise: «Spoiling on purpose is a small meanness that needs a "sorry".» What does the word "sorry" tell you about meanness? | *It is an unkind act that hurts someone | It is a happy present | It is a kind of game | It is a sport
test: «Understanding why someone is mean does not make the meanness okay, but it can change how you respond.» What does this sentence say? | *Knowing why someone is unkind does not excuse it, but it can change how you react | Meanness only happens to grown-ups | Being mean is always fine | Understanding someone makes them stop being unkind
test: «Real predators hunt to eat, not out of anger or meanness, and many fail more hunts than they win.» Why do real predators hunt? | To spread meanness to new animals | *To eat, not from unkindness | Because they are angry with other animals | To win trophies
exam: Which sense of meanness is shown when a child refuses to share their money with a friend who has none? | Being unkind with words | Being bored in class | Being very tall | *Being stingy, not wanting to share money
